      "title": "[MEM0-2026-01] mem0 self-hosted server: broken tenant authorization on memory endpoints",
      "descriptions": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "value": "mem0 2.2.1 self-hosted REST API authenticates callers but does not authorize them against the memory namespace or record they address. Every memory endpoint accepts a caller-supplied user_id, agent_id, run_id or memory id with no ownership check. The only role gate (unfiltered GET /memories, 403 for role=user) is bypassed by supplying any identifier. A role=user key can enumerate all tenants via GET /entities and then read, overwrite or delete other tenants' memories via GET /memories?user_id=, GET/PUT/DELETE /memories/{id}, GET /memories/{id}/history and POST /search."
        }
      ],
